/* -------------------------------------------------------------------
 * wrom1 -- TT_1p8V_25C
 * AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/rom_char/gen_rom_lib.py -- DO NOT EDIT
 *
 * The OpenRAM ROM compiler does not write a .lib; this file was built
 * from the LEF pins plus the circuit structure extracted from wrom1.sp.
 *
 * Model: precharged NAND-style (series chain) ROM, NO output latch.
 *   clk0 = 0 -> bitlines precharge (dout0 all ones)
 *   clk0 = 1 -> evaluate; the selected cells discharge the bitline
 *   worst case through ~88 series NMOS (column 214);
 *   dout0 valid 15.811 ns later
 *   dout0 becomes INVALID when clk0 falls. The consumer must either
 *   sample on clk0's falling edge, or drive the macro with an inverted
 *   clock (clk0 = ~clk) and capture on the system clock's rising edge.
 *   That invalidation IS in the data: bus(dout0) carries a second
 *   timing() group with timing_type : falling_edge and a delay of
 *   2.4992 ns (clk0 falling -> dout0 leaving its valid level).
 *   It is the EARLIEST invalidation -- t_clk2pre + t_pre_50 +
 *   t_bl2dout at the smallest load -- because what must be proven
 *   is that the consumer captured BEFORE the data went away.
 *
 * SOURCE: access/t_pre come from ngspice measurements on real Magic parasitic C + that corner's OWN sky130 models; 134x256 array, worst column 214 (series NMOS 88); front end + periphery power char/periph_{active,idle}_tt.log, bitline char/col214_worst_case_parasitic.log, back end + slew char/backend_tt_*.log, leakage char/col214_leak_tt.log, column energy char/col214_energy_tt.log
 * -- THIS corner (TT_1p8V_25C) was simulated separately with its own
 * sky130 model files (tt/ss/ff); no fixed scaling factor was used.
 * Measurement showed that this matters: the old SS x1.85 assumption was
 * 33% optimistic against the x2.76 that was actually measured.
 * Without --access/--t-pre this script falls back to analytic defaults
 * (based on a wrong NOR model) -- for sign-off ALWAYS call it with
 * measured values, i.e. through regen_rom_libs.sh.
 *
 * ACCESS IS THE SUM OF THREE TERMS (all measured):
 *   clk0 -> precharge/wordline : 0.7586 ns
 *   precharge -> bitline 50%   : 15.8106 ns
 *   bitline -> dout0           : 1.4933 .. 1.7300 ns (vs output load)
 *   TOTAL (worst load)         : 18.2992 ns
 * The back-end term covers the bitline inverter, the 256:32 column
 * mux and the output buffer.
 *
 * BOTH AXES OF THE TABLE ARE MEASURED.
 *   index_2 (output load)  : the back-end term, 1.4933 .. 1.7300 ns
 *   index_1 (clk0 slew)    : the front-end term, 0.7227 .. 0.7586 ns
 *     at clk0 transitions 0.05, 0.2, 0.5 ns
 * t_front is the only term that depends on the clk0 edge: the
 * bitline measurement triggers off the internal precharge net and
 * the back end is driven by the bitline, so neither can see clk0.
 * That is also why the output transition table stays flat along
 * index_1.
 * max_transition on the inputs is 0.5 ns, the top of that axis --
 * the library cannot declare a slew it was never measured at.
 *
 * EARLY PATH (retain_rise/retain_fall on dout0): dout0 keeps the
 * PREVIOUS cycle's value for 2.7234 .. 2.7593 ns after clk0 rises.
 * Measured on the FASTEST ARRAY this geometry can hold, where
 * everything else in this file uses the worst column. A stored 0
 * is a metal strap and leaves the series path; a stored 1 is a
 * transistor in it, so the discharge speed is set by the CONTENTS.
 * The bound therefore comes from the limit case -- every data
 * cell strapped out, with only the foot transistor left in series
 * -- and stays valid if this geometry is reprogrammed. At that
 * limit the bound is set by the fixed circuitry (foot transistor,
 * precharge PMOS, bitline wire and inverter) rather than by the
 * array, which is why it must be measured per macro but not
 * per .bin. Without it the tool believes the old data is held
 * right up to the access time and a race that eats it before the
 * capture flop takes it passes silently: a hold check has nothing
 * to fail on.
 * retaining_rise/fall is the smallest-load output slew, not a
 * separate measurement.
 * Output transition time MEASURED: 0.5036 .. 0.7746 ns
 *
 * POWER MODEL: internal_power on clk0 is ENERGY PER CYCLE (pJ);
 * the power tool applies the frequency (P = E*f*activity).
 *   when "cs0"  = 140.5111 pJ  (read: column array + periphery)
 *   when "!cs0" = 3.5426 pJ  (IDLE: cs0 only gates the
 *     precharge; the clk_int tree, the address buffers, the row
 *     decoder and 134 wordlines switch even when deselected.
 *     Leave this block out and OpenSTA silently scores it 0.)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
library (wrom1_TT_1p8V_25C) {
    delay_model : "table_lookup";
